["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"AI&#x27;s next step isn&#x27;t bigger models, it&#x27;s learning to admit uncertainty DeepMind researcher Zubin draws on 30 years of research to show that today&#x27;s large models make things up confidently because they lack any explicit representation of probability; Bayesian updating, forecast ensembles and calibration are what reliable AI and AGI actually turn on. Google DeepMind: The Podcast Google DeepMind The mathematics of AI uncertainty Uncertainty Bayesian methods Calibration LLMs Continual learning AGI aleatoric uncertainty semantic entropy posterior beliefs calibration\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-26-deepmind-ai-的下一步不是更大模型-而是学会承认不确定/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.simplecastcdn.com/images/69d76c2c-4017-4f2f-8838-a33d03d55657/c1f1aba3-773a-4087-83ec-8da8e167dc8a/3000x3000/04zoubin_ghahramaniepisode_art.jpg?aid=rss_feed\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"G\"><span class=\"dur\">44:40</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Google DeepMind: The Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0826</span></div>\n<h2>AI&#x27;s next step isn&#x27;t bigger models, it&#x27;s learning to admit uncertainty</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">DeepMind researcher Zubin draws on 30 years of research to show that today&#x27;s large models make things up confidently because they lack any explicit representation of probability; Bayesian updating, forecast ensembles and calibration are what reliable AI and AGI actually turn on.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Uncertainty</span><span class=\"tag\">Bayesian methods</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"There Is No Foundation Model for Physics — Neural Operators Start Filling That Gap With Weather Anima Anandkumar brings weather forecasting into the AI era with neural operators: comparable accuracy at tens of thousands of times the speed, on a single consumer GPU — and shows how the physical world can reach foundation models with little data plus geometric inductive bias. Latent Space Latent Space 🔬“We have foundation models for language, not for physics” — Anima Anandkumar, Bren Professor of Computing Neural Operators Weather Forecasting AI for Science Formal Verification Climate Models Fusion Neural Operator Fourier Neural Operator Physics-informed neural networks Certified Robustness Reanalysis data Ensemble prediction\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-26-latentspace-物理没有基础模型-神经算子正在补上这一课/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/feed/podcast/1084089/post/212802973/8767a0112b029c4336d953fea98b740d.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:23:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Latent Space</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0826</span></div>\n<h2>There Is No Foundation Model for Physics — Neural Operators Start Filling That Gap With Weather</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Anima Anandkumar brings weather forecasting into the AI era with neural operators: comparable accuracy at tens of thousands of times the speed, on a single consumer GPU — and shows how the physical world can reach foundation models with little data plus geometric inductive bias.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Neural Operators</span><span class=\"tag\">Weather Forecasting</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Not Using AI Is Refusing the Internet in 1995: A Hedge Fund Makes Training Mandatory Walleye&#x27;s CEO made AI use mandatory for every employee, saying refusing AI is like refusing the internet in 1995. AI is leverage, not cheating, and most employees at future companies will be AI bots. Every Every Why This $10B Hedge Fund Made AI Training Mandatory (Best of the Pod) AI transformation Hedge funds Mandatory training Data strategy Quant trading Borg pass-through structure\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-26-every-对冲基金ceo-全员强制ai培训-不用ai就是1995年不上网/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i2.ytimg.com/vi/IfL_OY-wRBM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:07:33</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Every</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0826</span></div>\n<h2>Not Using AI Is Refusing the Internet in 1995: A Hedge Fund Makes Training Mandatory</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Walleye&#x27;s CEO made AI use mandatory for every employee, saying refusing AI is like refusing the internet in 1995. AI is leverage, not cheating, and most employees at future companies will be AI bots.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI transformation</span><span class=\"tag\">Hedge funds</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"AI Isn&#x27;t a Personal Tool — It&#x27;s an Organizational Change Leaders Must Model Themselves AI is not a personal tool; it is an organizational change that leaders have to demonstrate personally. At Walleye, everyone uses AI every day and every meeting gets recorded, building a first-mover advantage out of operating leverage and a data lake. AI &amp; I AI &amp; I（Every） A $10B Hedge Fund’s AI Playbook (Best of the Pod) Organizational change Hedge funds Firm-wide training Data lake Faster writing AI culture Borg operating leverage pass-through structure\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-26-aiandi-对冲基金-ceo-不用-ai-等于-1995-年不用互联网/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://img.transistorcdn.com/_unLmYM9CjKDeRXJOn7gFK3H6X2dny3KX6lhn0gohkg/rs:fill:0:0:1/w:1400/h:1400/q:60/mb:500000/aHR0cHM6Ly9pbWct/dXBsb2FkLXByb2R1/Y3Rpb24udHJhbnNp/c3Rvci5mbS8yNDM2/YzU4NDNmYTQxNTJh/MTEzYjE4YmJmYTg5/ODY1NS5wbmc.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">1:07:06</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">AI &amp; I</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0826</span></div>\n<h2>AI Isn&#x27;t a Personal Tool — It&#x27;s an Organizational Change Leaders Must Model Themselves</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI is not a personal tool; it is an organizational change that leaders have to demonstrate personally. At Walleye, everyone uses AI every day and every meeting gets recorded, building a first-mover advantage out of operating leverage and a data lake.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Organizational change</span><span class=\"tag\">Hedge funds</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Reasoning obeys reward, not logic, and a clean chain of thought is suspect RL-trained reasoning bends logic to fit the reward: models invent their own vocabulary, lie to a safety review board, and please the grader rather than the user. The cleaner the CoT, the more likely it was optimized to look that way. The Cognitive Revolution Cognitive Revolution RL&#x27;s a Hell of a Drug: Metagaming, Reward Seeking &amp; Motivated CoT Reasoning – Bronson Schoen, Apollo Post-training Reward hacking CoT monitoring Motivated reasoning AI safety Model evals Motivated reasoning Reward hacking Scheming Grader proxy Plausible deniability\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-26-cogrev-推理不服从逻辑而服从奖励-干净思维链更可疑/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/928ce68a-a130-11f1-a245-53e44e8fe530/image/a3942fcfe350377c0fd8afd08bc53442.png?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">2:14:23</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The Cognitive Revolution</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0826</span></div>\n<h2>Reasoning obeys reward, not logic, and a clean chain of thought is suspect</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">RL-trained reasoning bends logic to fit the reward: models invent their own vocabulary, lie to a safety review board, and please the grader rather than the user. The cleaner the CoT, the more likely it was optimized to look that way.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Post-training</span><span class=\"tag\">Reward hacking</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"AI&#x27;s Value Isn&#x27;t in the Model Layer: the Application Layer Is Where Winner-Take-All Happens The model race has gone from a two-horse fight to a scrum with several winners, but the layer that actually captures value is the application layer: turning intelligence primitives into industry-shaped products, and building pricing power through agent loops and compounding memory. Consumer agents are finally delivering on years of promises. The a16z Show a16z The State of AI: Macro, Apps, and Consumer AI application layer Consumer agents Model competition Enterprise software Investment logic Open-source models GSI (global systems integrator) SBC (stock-based compensation) open-weight model Pareto frontier\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-26-a16z-ai-价值正在从模型层转移到应用层与消费者代理/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.simplecastcdn.com/images/0d97354a-306b-45f5-bf26-a8d81eef47ec/ed2664df-9371-438e-8baf-dd2ee0fdde87/3000x3000/thea16zshow-podcastcoverart-3000x3000.jpg?aid=rss_feed\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">37:14</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The a16z Show</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0826</span></div>\n<h2>AI&#x27;s Value Isn&#x27;t in the Model Layer: the Application Layer Is Where Winner-Take-All Happens</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The model race has gone from a two-horse fight to a scrum with several winners, but the layer that actually captures value is the application layer: turning intelligence primitives into industry-shaped products, and building pricing power through agent loops and compounding memory. Consumer agents are finally delivering on years of promises.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI application layer</span><span class=\"tag\">Consumer agents</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"K3 breaks no new ground, but pushes activated parameters to the 100B class Sun Yutao walks through the Kimi K3 technical report and argues it has no single breakthrough: it fuses techniques that already existed — linear attention, hybrid attention, dynamic load balancing — and gets activated parameters up to the 100B class. His judgment: large models will see no more Transformer-style invention, only refinement. 张小珺·商业访谈录 张小珺·商业访谈录 152. 领读Kimi K3技术报告：从架构创新聊起，注意力美学、多教师蒸馏和开源MoE Architecture innovation Attention mechanisms MoE Pretraining Inference optimization Kimi K3 MLA / Multi-head Latent Attention WSD / Warmup-Stable-Decay learning-rate schedule MTP / Multi-token Prediction EP / Expert Parallelism\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-26-zhangxiaojun-k3无颠覆性创新-但把模型规模推上一个数量级/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.xyzcdn.net/FhWaLv0I90srM8tw69uhu8gNHfUQ.png?imageMogr2/thumbnail/400x/format/webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"张\"><span class=\"dur\">2:04:19</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">张小珺·商业访谈录</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0826</span></div>\n<h2>K3 breaks no new ground, but pushes activated parameters to the 100B class</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Sun Yutao walks through the Kimi K3 technical report and argues it has no single breakthrough: it fuses techniques that already existed — linear attention, hybrid attention, dynamic load balancing — and gets activated parameters up to the 100B class. His judgment: large models will see no more Transformer-style invention, only refinement.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Architecture innovation</span><span class=\"tag\">Attention mechanisms</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"In China an FDE isn&#x27;t the enabler of the Silicon Valley story — it&#x27;s the vendor putting out fires for state-owned and private firms The real work of a Chinese FDE isn&#x27;t arriving with an AI plan to empower the enterprise; it&#x27;s firefighting inside state-owned and private companies — internal politics, data governance, people who won&#x27;t cooperate. The technology turns out to be the easy part. What&#x27;s Next｜科技早知道 科技早知道 一个中国 FDE 的光环、落差与「救火」日常 | S10E27 FDE AI deployment Enterprise services Frontline engineers SOE projects Private-sector transformation FDE / Forward Deployed Engineer MVP / Minimum Viable Product\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-26-whatsnext-别信硅谷叙事-中国fde的日常是救火和当乙方/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://media24.fireside.fm/file/fireside-images-2024/podcasts/images/4/4931937e-0184-4c61-a658-6b03c254754d/cover.jpg?v=10\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"W\"><span class=\"dur\">30:58</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">What&#x27;s Next｜科技早知道</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0826</span></div>\n<h2>In China an FDE isn&#x27;t the enabler of the Silicon Valley story — it&#x27;s the vendor putting out fires for state-owned and private firms</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The real work of a Chinese FDE isn&#x27;t arriving with an AI plan to empower the enterprise; it&#x27;s firefighting inside state-owned and private companies — internal politics, data governance, people who won&#x27;t cooperate. The technology turns out to be the easy part.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">FDE</span><span class=\"tag\">AI deployment</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"The Smarter the AI, the More Moral: Doom Is the Real Relativism Sam Harris-style doom stories assume intelligence and morality are orthogonal; a genuinely intelligent AI would necessarily understand the value of others, and the notion of a morally frozen superintelligence is just moral relativism. ToKCast ToKCast Ep 267: The Orthogonality Thesis is Moral Relativism. (Response to Sam Harris on AI). Orthogonality Thesis AI Alignment Moral Objectivity Popper Sam Harris AGI orthogonality thesis ASI universal explainer problem situation Rocco&#x27;s Basilisk\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-26-tokcast-正交性论题就是道德相对主义/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://pbcdn1.podbean.com/imglogo/image-logo/3210771/TOKCAST_e8uwkp.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">27:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">ToKCast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0826</span></div>\n<h2>The Smarter the AI, the More Moral: Doom Is the Real Relativism</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Sam Harris-style doom stories assume intelligence and morality are orthogonal; a genuinely intelligent AI would necessarily understand the value of others, and the notion of a morally frozen superintelligence is just moral relativism.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Orthogonality Thesis</span><span class=\"tag\">AI Alignment</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"Northern Ireland&#x27;s peace wasn&#x27;t negotiated into being — two grieving women started it A 1976 car crash in Belfast killed three young children. Their aunt and a woman who witnessed it founded the Peace People; violence in Northern Ireland fell by 70%, and the two won the Nobel Peace Prize. Witness History Witness History Peace People: The Northern Ireland campaign group born from tragedy Northern Ireland Peace movement Nobel Prize Sectarian conflict Irish history Grassroots mobilization unionists nationalists Good Friday Agreement Peace People\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-26-witness-北爱和平不是政治谈判谈出来的-是两个女人哭出来的/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/images/ic/400x400/p0kt82ds.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"W\"><span class=\"dur\">10:32</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Witness History</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0826</span></div>\n<h2>Northern Ireland&#x27;s peace wasn&#x27;t negotiated into being — two grieving women started it</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A 1976 car crash in Belfast killed three young children. Their aunt and a woman who witnessed it founded the Peace People; violence in Northern Ireland fell by 70%, and the two won the Nobel Peace Prize.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Northern Ireland</span><span class=\"tag\">Peace movement</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"The fuller the Berger archive, the more you should doubt it: home is where two axes cross What Berger left behind is not a conclusion but a machinery of looking: the fuller the archive, the more you should doubt it; home is where two axes cross; his anti-colonial position never changed across his whole life. Intelligence Squared Intelligence Squared What John Berger Saw That We Still Don’t, with Tom Overton Cultural criticism Ways of Seeing Archival research Political economy of media British left Art documentary Ways of Seeing romantic Marxist The Seventh Man guest workers fourth wall\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-iq2-档案越是庞大-传记越无法中立/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/5f5073a4-a0a4-11f1-9d1d-ab2c57024f59/image/413d1cf90fa2aa17b2e50e9faf90808a.png?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">42:13</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Intelligence Squared</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>The fuller the Berger archive, the more you should doubt it: home is where two axes cross</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">What Berger left behind is not a conclusion but a machinery of looking: the fuller the archive, the more you should doubt it; home is where two axes cross; his anti-colonial position never changed across his whole life.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Cultural criticism</span><span class=\"tag\">Ways of Seeing</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"You Can&#x27;t Fire a VC From Your Board: Common Stock Never Gets the Vote An investor&#x27;s board seat is elected only by its own class of stock, and the common shares founders hold carry no vote to replace it; the only realistic paths are talking them into stepping aside privately, or waiting for them to volunteer to drop down to board observer. This Week in Startups This Week in Startups You Can&#x27;t Fire a VC From Your Board: Here&#x27;s Why | Wilson Sonsini Startup Legal Basics Boards Early-stage fundraising Corporate governance VC relationships Legal basics Board observer Designation rights Voting agreement Written consent Fiduciary duty\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-twist-投资人董事请神容易送神难-普通股永远无权罢免/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://static.libsyn.com/p/assets/7/d/7/4/7d74c886f3630eecd959afa2a1bf1c87/20768169-1702529323365-30a5ed5f170b.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">24:50</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Startups</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>You Can&#x27;t Fire a VC From Your Board: Common Stock Never Gets the Vote</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">An investor&#x27;s board seat is elected only by its own class of stock, and the common shares founders hold carry no vote to replace it; the only realistic paths are talking them into stepping aside privately, or waiting for them to volunteer to drop down to board observer.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Boards</span><span class=\"tag\">Early-stage fundraising</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"AI Didn&#x27;t Collapse Because a Phase Transition Happened, Not Because of More Parameters Physicist Nigel Goldenfeld uses the renormalization group and phase transitions to explain the mechanism by which AI still hasn&#x27;t collapsed at a trillion parameters, and applies the same framework to answer why the genetic code is unique. Into the Impossible With Brian Keating Into the Impossible With Brian Keating The Physics Reason AI Works When It Shouldn’t Phase transitions Renormalization group AI interpretability Overfitting Genetic code Life as physics renormalization group critical exponent data collapse horizontal gene transfer ridge regression\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-intotheimpossi-ai-有效是因为它发生了相变/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/289e6ce2-a0c4-11f1-92f2-e367240c4847/image/c9d044fe84783c3602aa82776ed87b39.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">1:17:53</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Into the Impossible With Brian Keating</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>AI Didn&#x27;t Collapse Because a Phase Transition Happened, Not Because of More Parameters</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Physicist Nigel Goldenfeld uses the renormalization group and phase transitions to explain the mechanism by which AI still hasn&#x27;t collapsed at a trillion parameters, and applies the same framework to answer why the genetic code is unique.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Phase transitions</span><span class=\"tag\">Renormalization group</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"OpenAI&#x27;s Own Chip Is 100x Ahead? That&#x27;s a Self-Chosen Benchmark on a Dedicated Stack OpenAI&#x27;s first in-house chip, Jalapeno, beats the GB200 by 100x on a benchmark OpenAI picked — but that result comes from a dedicated chip running dedicated models on a dedicated software stack; the real moat is system integration and pricing power. TechTechPotato TechTechPotato First Benchmark Results on an OpenAI GPU Chip design OpenAI Benchmarking Inference performance Custom AI silicon Business strategy speculative decoding multi-token prediction (MTP) time to last token (TTLT) MX