pute is concentrating into two labs several times over each year, and by 2028 they will control most of the world&#x27;s compute</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Compute is concentrating into Anthropic and OpenAI at a rate of several times a year; by 2028 they will control most of the world&#x27;s effective compute, may push the price of compute to $50 million per megawatt, and could trigger a sovereign debt crisis.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Compute</span><span class=\"tag\">Lab economics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Rack Radiation Over the Limit: Two Rounds of Debugging Failed, and the Fix Was Hiding at an Unrelated Conference Radiation at 26.565GHz off the back of the rack came in over the limit. Two rounds of troubleshooting turned up nothing, and the fix finally came from a paper presented at an unrelated conference: add absorber material at the connector. This is not black magic, it is high-frequency physics. Oxide and Friends Oxide and Friends The Return to the Chamber of Mysteries EMC Hardware engineering Rack servers Optical transceivers Compliance testing EMC (electromagnetic compatibility) Slot antenna Grounded coplanar waveguide QSFP cage Line (EMC chamber)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-oxide-emc-合规是玄学吗-一次机架级辐射超标排障记/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://img.transistorcdn.com/vXnd7VnDMA2AeXtSnRyFBM54tRuYH_AaVfaVeYg8QmA/rs:fill:0:0:1/w:1400/h:1400/q:60/mb:500000/aHR0cHM6Ly9pbWct/dXBsb2FkLXByb2R1/Y3Rpb24udHJhbnNp/c3Rvci5mbS9hMWM0/ZDJiYmNhOTJkMDMz/NTVmNTEzOGM3M2Vl/M2FkNi5wbmc.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">1:16:08</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Oxide and Friends</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>Rack Radiation Over the Limit: Two Rounds of Debugging Failed, and the Fix Was Hiding at an Unrelated Conference</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Radiation at 26.565GHz off the back of the rack came in over the limit. Two rounds of troubleshooting turned up nothing, and the fix finally came from a paper presented at an unrelated conference: add absorber material at the connector. This is not black magic, it is high-frequency physics.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">EMC</span><span class=\"tag\">Hardware engineering</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"AI Turns Software From an Engineering Constraint Into a Capital One Martin Casado and Steven Sinofsky&#x27;s central claim: AI has moved software from an engineering constraint to a capital constraint — a team of 20 can now effectively spend a billion dollars, which is why startups can compete head-on with the incumbents. The a16z Show a16z The New Economics of AI | Martin Casado &amp; Steven Sinofsky Compute Capital Startups Venture Capital AI Economics Incumbent Competition Foom / fast takeoff TAM / Total Addressable Market in-distribution Mythical man-month expert systems\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-a16z-ai-正在把工程问题变成资本问题/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.simplecastcdn.com/images/0d97354a-306b-45f5-bf26-a8d81eef47ec/ed2664df-9371-438e-8baf-dd2ee0fdde87/3000x3000/thea16zshow-podcastcoverart-3000x3000.jpg?aid=rss_feed\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:03:32</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The a16z Show</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>AI Turns Software From an Engineering Constraint Into a Capital One</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Martin Casado and Steven Sinofsky&#x27;s central claim: AI has moved software from an engineering constraint to a capital constraint — a team of 20 can now effectively spend a billion dollars, which is why startups can compete head-on with the incumbents.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Compute</span><span class=\"tag\">Capital</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Administrative Humiliation Is Why the Poor Hate Government: Applying for Benefits Is a Time Tax Administrative burden in government benefit programs is not an efficiency problem but an instrument of social control: it punishes the poor with humiliation and paperwork, turns progressive policy into a funnel that screens out all but a few, and ends by making recipients hate the government. The Ezra Klein Show Ezra Klein Show This Is Why People Hate the Government Welfare state Administrative burden Time tax Medicaid Tax reform American politics time tax ordeal mechanism improper payment only-once policy\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-ezra-时间税-行政羞辱是穷人恨政府的原因/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.simplecastcdn.com/images/47913775-afcf-4643-935f-31f1dcc86cfb/6a0e5e15-04a3-47c8-9c50-2f2fe8e84437/3000x3000/teks-album-20art-3000px.jpg?aid=rss_feed\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:17:28</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Ezra Klein Show</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>Administrative Humiliation Is Why the Poor Hate Government: Applying for Benefits Is a Time Tax</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Administrative burden in government benefit programs is not an efficiency problem but an instrument of social control: it punishes the poor with humiliation and paperwork, turns progressive policy into a funnel that screens out all but a few, and ends by making recipients hate the government.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b>